From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 17:21:31 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(gateway): a boundary handoff resumes the stored call,
 keeps admission open and takes over sooner

gateway.restart_turn_handoff_boundary, three fixes from a live rollout.

The next gateway ran a new model call for a turn handed off with a parked clarify or approval (or before its tool round) instead of the stored tool call: the transcript load's alternation repair, and then the gateway replay cleanup, treated the turn's unanswered last tool calls as a crash orphan (dropped when read-only, answered with an "effect unknown" notice otherwise). The resume of a handed-off turn now repairs and cleans only the rows before the turn's input row; the turn's own rows reach the agent as stored, so the stored call runs once under its tool_use id.

New input waited for the next gateway during the whole boundary wait (up to the slowest running turn's next boundary). Now new turns keep starting on this gateway while the turns that were running when the restart began reach their boundaries; then admission closes as before and the turns started meanwhile are handed over at their next boundary. A turn handed off here is never claimed again here. API runs (not handed off) stay refused from the restart request.

The standby polls the profile lock every 20 ms instead of 200 ms, and the boundary wait checks every 50 ms instead of 100 ms.
